{
  "comment": "Each case is a JSON text and what JavaScript's JSON.stringify(JSON.parse(input)) writes for it, recorded from Node.js: an object's members with the keys that are array indexes first, ascending, then the rest as written, numbers as the double the literal reads as, and strings with JavaScript's escapes. Each literal is one serde_json reads as the double JavaScript does with its arbitrary_precision feature and without (no literal past u64 written as an integer, which serde_json's default reader may round to a neighbouring double). Every Rust copy of JSON.stringify must agree: superschematic-engine's json::stringify, superschematic-rules-behaviors' derived stringify and superschematic-schema-ir's jsjson::stringify.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "input": "{\"b\": 1, \"2\": true, \"a\": null, \"1\": \"x\", \"01\": [], \"4294967295\": 0, \"4294967294\": -1}",
      "output": "{\"1\":\"x\",\"2\":true,\"4294967294\":-1,\"b\":1,\"a\":null,\"01\":[],\"4294967295\":0}"
    },
    {
      "input": "{\"a\": {}, \"b\": 1.0, \"10\": [true, null, 1e21], \"2\": \"q\\\"\\u0001<\u2028\"}",
      "output": "{\"2\":\"q\\\"\\u0001<\u2028\",\"10\":[true,null,1e+21],\"a\":{},\"b\":1}"
    },
    {
      "input": "{\"b\": 1.0, \"2\": [true, null, 0.5], \"a\": \"x\\n\"}",
      "output": "{\"2\":[true,null,0.5],\"b\":1,\"a\":\"x\\n\"}"
    },
    {
      "input": "{\"lat\": 1.5, \"lon\": -0.0, \"zero\": -0}",
      "output": "{\"lat\":1.5,\"lon\":0,\"zero\":0}"
    },
    {
      "input": "{\"x\": {\"1\": [], \"0\": {\"b\": 2, \"a\": 1}}, \"\": \"\", \"-1\": 0, \"1.5\": 0, \" 1\": 0}",
      "output": "{\"x\":{\"0\":{\"b\":2,\"a\":1},\"1\":[]},\"\":\"\",\"-1\":0,\"1.5\":0,\" 1\":0}"
    },
    {
      "input": "\"tab\\t quote\\\" slash\\\\ \\u0001 \u2028 \u2029 \u00e9 \ud83d\ude00 <>&\"",
      "output": "\"tab\\t quote\\\" slash\\\\ \\u0001 \u2028 \u2029 \u00e9 \ud83d\ude00 <>&\""
    },
    {
      "input": "\"\\b\\f\\n\\r\\t\\u0000\\u001f\\u007f\\/\"",
      "output": "\"\\b\\f\\n\\r\\t\\u0000\\u001f\u007f/\""
    },
    {
      "input": "[1.0, 1e2, 1E-7, 12345678901234567890, 9007199254740993, -9007199254740993]",
      "output": "[1,100,1e-7,12345678901234567000,9007199254740992,-9007199254740992]"
    },
    {
      "input": "[0.1, 0.000001, 0.0000001, 1.5e-7, 1.2345678901234568e20, 1e21, 1.5e300, -2.5e-10, 5e-324, 1.7976931348623157e308, 100, 1e20, 0.30000000000000004]",
      "output": "[0.1,0.000001,1e-7,1.5e-7,123456789012345680000,1e+21,1.5e+300,-2.5e-10,5e-324,1.7976931348623157e+308,100,100000000000000000000,0.30000000000000004]"
    },
    {
      "input": "[[], {}, [[{}]], null, true, false, \"\"]",
      "output": "[[],{},[[{}]],null,true,false,\"\"]"
    }
  ]
}
